- content_for :title, "Analytics acquisition"

- extra = capture do
  - if @channel_mix
    = render layout: "shared/card", locals: {id: "channel-mix", title: "Channel mix by #{@channel_mix[:unit]}", icon: "bar-chart", class: "mb-6"} do
      %div{class: "px-4 py-3"}
        = analytics_channel_mix_chart(@channel_mix)
      %p{class: "border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-500"}
        The period's five busiest channels keep the same colour in every bar, so a channel growing or shrinking shows
        even when sessions overall don't change.

  - if @campaign_results&.any?
    = render layout: "shared/card", locals: {id: "campaign-results", title: "What each campaign brought", icon: "bar-chart", class: "mb-6"} do
      %div{class: "px-4 py-3"}
        = analytics_campaign_chart(@campaign_results, @period)
      %p{class: "border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-500"}
        Each campaign's links and sources added together. Key events are the ones marked in Google Analytics, so a campaign that reads zero may simply not have led to one.

= render "google/shared/report", title: "Analytics acquisition", extra: extra,
  description: "Where readers come from: what first brought them, and the channels, sources and sites behind each visit, from Google Analytics. GA keeps processing late hits for up to two days."
